{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Will your wealth avail</b> — it is the wealth, and the owner of wealth is called שוע, as in 'if they cry out — will he give them שוע' (Job 27:9), and the sense is: will your wealth avail." "<b>and not distress</b> — and the sense is: distress will not avail, neither wealth nor all who exert strength. And surely you see that 'תשאף' is not [from the root] לילה, and the tav is feminine, as we find מקום — in one instance feminine — so that 'מאמצי כח' is lowered and peoples rise up beneath them."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "The text is obscure: the argument about לילה, the feminine מקום, and 'peoples rising up' is cryptic and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:43.799213173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}